00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:51.540
Okay.
好的。

164
00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:52.880
So I hit the record button.
所以我按下了录音按钮。

165
00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:53.070
Yeah.
嗯。

166
00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:54.240
And I was like, let's do this.
然后我说，开始吧。

167
00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.340
I'm feeling like this isn't going where we're hoping.
我感觉事情的发展没按我们预想的来。

168
00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.540
Okay, Dave and I talked for half an hour.
好吧，我和戴夫聊了半个小时。

169
00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:58.860
Yeah.
嗯。

170
00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:00.760
I have 30 minutes.
我有30分钟的录像。

171
00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:01.220
Okay.
好的。

172
00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.300
Of me filming my screen.
是我录制屏幕的视频。

173
00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:03.960
Yeah.
嗯。

174
00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:04.880
With no sound.
但是没有声音。

175
00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:05.380
Okay.
好吧。

176
00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:05.900
Okay.
好吧。

177
00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.120
It's a record button.
那是个录屏按钮。

178
00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.060
How was I supposed to know it doesn't record sound?
我怎么会知道它不录声音呢？

179
00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:12.040
I don't know where to begin with this one, Angela.
安吉拉，我真不知道该从哪儿说起。

180
00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:13.540
Is it because I'm 100 years old?
是因为我年纪大到一百岁了吗？

181
00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:19.300
Well, it's just that that's sort of like when my mom wrote me my first email.
好吧，这就像我妈第一次给我写邮件时的情况一样。

182
00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:20.020
Yeah.
嗯。

183
00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:25.140
She called me on the phone and said, why haven't you responded to my email that I sent you?
她打电话给我说，为什么没回我发给你的邮件？

184
00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:25.500
Yeah.
嗯。

185
00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.560
And I said, well, I never got your email.
我说，我没收到你的邮件啊。

186
00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:30.560
What email address did you send it to?
你发到哪个邮箱地址了？

187
00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.780
And she said, I sent it to you.
她说，我发给你了。

188
00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:32.680
I sent it to Jenna.
我发给珍娜了。

189
00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.960
And I said, I don't understand.
我说，我不明白。

190
00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:39.260
And she said, I opened the email box and it said to, and I wrote Jenna.
她说，我打开邮件框，上面写着“收件人”，我就写了珍娜。

191
00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.220
She just sent an email to Jenna.
她只是给珍娜发了一封邮件。

192
00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:46.240
That is very similar to what you've done here with the record button on your phone.
这和你手机上那个录屏按钮的操作非常相似。

193
00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.180
A little bit.
有一点点。

194
00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:47.900
Come on now.
得了吧。

195
00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:48.340
A little bit.
有一点点。

196
00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.020
Wait a minute.
等一下。

197
00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:49.780
It's kind of.
差不多吧。

198
00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:51.320
Anyway, whatever, guys.
总之，不管怎样，伙计们。

199
00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:56.680
The long story short here is, Dave, thank you so much for talking to me last night for half an hour.
长话短说，戴夫，非常感谢你昨晚和我聊了半个小时。

200
00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:00.640
And I wrote down everything we talked about because it didn't record.
我把我们聊的所有内容都记下来了，因为录音没录上。

201
00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:03.020
You do have a gazillion note cards today.
你今天准备的笔记卡片可真多啊。

202
00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:06.260
Angela had to move seats because she has so many note cards.
安吉拉不得不换个座位，因为她的笔记卡片太多了。

203
00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.420
I have so many note cards.
我有好多笔记卡片。

204
00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:11.320
I have lots of little fun tidbits from Dave, but I'll save those as we go.
我这儿还有很多关于戴夫的趣事，不过我们待会儿再说。

205
00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:11.720
Okay.
好的。

206
00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:12.320
That's great.
太棒了。

207
00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:19.280
Something I'd like to expand on is what you were saying about Steve Carell starting at Second City in Chicago.
我想展开聊聊你刚才提到的史蒂夫·卡瑞尔在芝加哥“第二城”喜剧团起步的事。

208
00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:26.220
I think a lot of people don't realize the long journey that a lot of us took before we landed on the office.
我觉得很多人都没意识到，我们在加入《办公室》之前都经历过漫长的奋斗历程。

209
00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.020
And in particular, Steve Carell.
尤其是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

210
00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:33.720
He was doing comedy in Chicago on Second City for a very, very long time.
他在芝加哥的“第二城”演了非常非常久的喜剧。

211
00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:40.040
And then he and his wife, Nancy, they moved to New York City because she had an audition for Saturday Night Live.
后来他和妻子南希搬到了纽约，因为南希要去参加《周六夜现场》的试镜。

212
00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:40.980
And she got it.
结果她被选上了。

213
00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:41.680
She did.
确实如此。

214
00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.600
And her and Dave were on Saturday Night Live together.
她和戴夫还一起上过《周六夜现场》呢。

215
00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:49.700
So they had known each other for a really long time and journeyed through quite a bit.
所以他们认识很久了，一起走过了不少风雨。

216
00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.200
And Steve was really excited.
史蒂夫当时特别兴奋。

217
00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:55.520
He is actually the one who pitched Dave to Greg for Todd Packer.
其实是他向格雷格推荐戴夫来演托德·帕克的。

218
00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:58.540
He was really like, you've got to cast Dave Koechner.
他当时极力推荐说，你一定要选戴夫·科恩查尔。

219
00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.520
They had just done Anchorman together.
他们刚一起拍完《王牌播音员》。

220
00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:04.460
And he just knew that they'd be off to the races and it'd be so much fun.
他知道他们俩搭档肯定会一拍即合，一定会非常有趣。

221
00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:07.120
And their dynamic in Anchorman was amazing.
他们在《王牌播音员》里的互动太精彩了。

222
00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:08.320
Their chemistry there was amazing.
他们的化学反应简直绝了。

223
00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:18.200
But it makes sense because they had been schlepping through Chicago to New York to LA together doing comedy for close to 15 years.
这也不奇怪，因为他们一起在芝加哥、纽约和洛杉矶摸爬滚打演了近15年的喜剧。

224
00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:18.680
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

225
00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.300
They'd known each other for so long.
他们认识太久了。

226
00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.000
And you were in those circles, Angela.
安吉拉，你当时也在那个圈子里吧。

227
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.060
Well, I never got into that.
呃，我从来没参与过那些。

228
00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:26.280
I never did the comedy improv sketch comedy thing.
我没搞过即兴喜剧或小品喜剧那一套。

229
00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:26.820
Yes.
是的。

230
00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:31.220
I had met Dave years ago at ImprovOlympic out here in Los Angeles.
我多年前在洛杉矶的“即兴奥林匹克”见过戴夫。

231
00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:32.140
It was called I.O.
当时叫I.O.

232
00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:32.540
WeSt.
西部分部。

233
00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:37.280
And he was part of a phenomenal improv show called Beer Shark Mice.
他当时是一个叫“啤酒鲨鱼鼠”的超赞即兴表演团的成员。

234
00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:38.760
These guys were amazing.
这些人太厉害了。

235
00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:40.700
They were like the best of the beSt.
他们简直是精英中的精英。

236
00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:42.180
It would sell out.
场场爆满。

237
00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:43.660
It would be standing room only.
连站票都卖光了。

238
00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.040
They were amazing.
他们太棒了。

239
00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:53.080
It was Mike Coleman, Pat Finn, Neil Flynn, and Pete Holney, Dave Koechner, and then also Paul Valancourt.
成员有迈克·科尔曼、帕特·芬恩、尼尔·弗林、皮特·霍尔尼、戴夫·科恩查尔，还有保罗·瓦兰考特。

240
00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:54.840
They were just phenomenal.
他们简直神了。

241
00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:55.300
Wow.
哇。

242
00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:56.100
What a show.
真是场精彩的演出。

243
00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:57.140
It was great.
确实很棒。

244
00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.900
So, like, listen, if you're an improv nerd out there, these guys are the best of the beSt.
所以，听着，如果你是个即兴表演迷，这些人绝对是顶尖高手。

245
00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.660
I was working in the light booth.
我当时在灯光控制室工作。

246
00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:04.840
I was in charge of calling their lights.
我负责给他们的表演打灯。

247
00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:11.820
And I was really intimidated because the person in the light booth makes it fade to black when you feel that the show has wrapped up.
我当时特别紧张，因为灯光师得在觉得演出结束时负责切断灯光。

248
00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:12.700
So what?
那又怎样？

249
00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.240
It's kind of on you to decide.
这得由你来决定什么时候结束。

250
00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:14.940
It's on me.
确实由我决定。

251
00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:15.980
And here I am like.
而我当时就像是。

252
00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:18.980
You're like the person lowering the curtain at the end of the show.
你就像是在演出结束时拉下帷幕的那个人。

253
00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:19.340
Yes.
没错。

254
00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.780
And I'm just like a newbie at the theater.
而我只是个剧院里的新手。

255
00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:22.960
Like, I'm like, really?
我就想，真的吗？

256
00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:23.940
You're going to trust me?
你真的要信任我吗？

257
00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:25.460
Was there no one else?
难道没有别人了吗？

258
00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.080
And so I was calling lights.
于是我负责喊灯光指令。

259
00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:31.240
And I really felt like the show wrapped up.
我当时真的觉得演出已经结束了。

260
00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.480
And it was about 30 minutes.
大概过了30分钟。

261
00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:34.060
And I pulled it to black.
我就把灯光切黑了。

262
00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:36.320
And they were like, what?
他们当时就问，怎么回事？

263
00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:41.360
And then afterwards, Dave and everyone was like, Ange, we had a whole other round to go.
事后，戴夫和其他人都说，安吉，我们还有整整一轮没演呢。

264
00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:43.520
You called the lights way too soon.
你切灯切得太早了。

265
00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.240
And I was like, I am so sorry.
我就说，我太抱歉了。

266
00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:46.280
I am so sorry.
我真的非常抱歉。

267
00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:47.200
I felt so horrible.
我当时感觉糟透了。

268
00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:47.980
All right.
好吧。

269
00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.440
So it's the next week.
到了下周。

270
00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:53.580
And Dave comes up to me and says, Ange, let us go about 45 minutes tonight.
戴夫走过来对我说，安吉，今晚让我们演45分钟左右。

271
00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:54.620
I'm like, okay, Dave.
我说，好的，戴夫。

272
00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:55.180
Got it.
明白了。

273
00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:56.120
Set my timer.
我设了个计时器。

274
00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:57.120
You set a timer.
你还设了计时器。

275
00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.060
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

276
00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:58.480
I set a timer.
我确实设了计时器。

277
00:09:58.480 --> 00:09:59.660
That's very Jenna of you.
这很珍娜风格。

278
00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:00.520
Thank you.
谢谢。

279
00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:00.940
Yes.
是的。

280
00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.200
I didn't want to get it wrong.
我不想再搞砸了。

281
00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:05.580
So anyway, I'm up in the light booth at 39 minutes.
总之，我在灯光控制室待到39分钟的时候。

282
00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.920
I thought they had their out, Jenna.
我以为他们已经演完了，珍娜。

283
00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:07.460
Okay.
好吧。

284
00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:08.660
I did not pull lights.
我没有切灯。

285
00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:09.020
You did.
你切了。

286
00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:09.440
No.
没有。

287
00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:10.000
No.
没有。

288
00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.300
And then they went to 45 minutes.
然后他们演到了45分钟。

289
00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.680
And then it was almost an hour.
接着快一个小时了。

290
00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:15.540
What?
什么？

291
00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:16.260
I didn't.
我没有。

292
00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:18.600
I was too nervous.
我太紧张了。

293
00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:19.240
I don't know.
我不知道。

294
00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:19.740
I froze.
我僵住了。

295
00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:22.760
They're probably just out there just flailing on stage.
他们可能就在台上不知所措地乱晃。

296
00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.380
It was getting awkward.
场面变得很尴尬。

297
00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:26.260
And Dave walks backstage.
然后戴夫走到后台。

298
00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:30.520
And someone had left, I don't know, a spare tire to like a truck or a Jeep.
有人留下了一个，我不知道，可能是卡车或吉普车的备用轮胎。

299
00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:31.220
It was enormous.
那东西巨大无比。

300
00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:37.380
So Dave gets this giant tire and he rolls it across the stage into the audience.
于是戴夫拿过那个巨大的轮胎，把它滚过舞台，滚向了观众席。

301
00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:39.920
And he's like, that's our show, you guys.
然后他说，伙计们，这就是我们的演出了。

302
00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:41.620
And I was like, oh, crap.
我当时就想，糟了。

303
00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:45.520
Wait, did you, when the tire went across the stage, did you finally go to Black Ange?
等等，当那个轮胎滚过舞台时，你最后去找Black Ange了吗？

304
00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:46.020
I did.
我去了。

305
00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:46.460
Okay.
好的。

306
00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.220
So you got his signal then.
那你收到他的信号了。

307
00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:48.620
I got it.
我收到了。

308
00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:49.180
I got it, Dave.
我收到了，Dave。

309
00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:49.680
The tire.
那个轮胎。

310
00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:50.220
I got it.
我收到了。

311
00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:51.040
And I went backstage.
然后我去了后台。

312
00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.140
I was like, you guys.
我当时说，你们这些人啊。

313
00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:55.280
And we all started cracking up and they still talk about it.
我们都笑得前仰后合，他们到现在还在谈论这件事。

314
00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.440
They still talk about the tire.
他们还在谈论那个轮胎。

315
00:10:56.980 --> 00:10:58.420
Anyway, I just love those guys so much.
总之，我真的很喜欢那帮家伙。

316
00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:02.520
And believe it or not, I did call lights for them a few more times until they got their
信不信由你，在他们找到正式人选之前，我还帮他们打过几次灯光。

317
00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:03.400
official person.
正式的人员。

318
00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:06.000
But that is how I met Dave Koechner.
但这就是我遇见Dave Koechner的方式。

319
00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:09.080
Didn't Greg Daniels go to a few of those shows?
Greg Daniels没去看过那几场演出吗？

320
00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.140
I mean, maybe not Dave's in particular, but.
我是说，也许不是Dave那场特别的演出，但是。

321
00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:12.020
Oh, no.
哦，没有。

322
00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:18.620
Greg loved supporting like small improv theaters and a lot of improvisers ended up on our show.
Greg很喜欢支持像小型即兴剧场这样的地方，很多即兴表演者最终都上了我们的节目。

323
00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:24.220
So I know Rainn Wilson would make fun of me, but I'd be like, oh, you know, whoever actor
所以我知道Rainn Wilson会取笑我，但我会说，哦，你知道的，不管哪个演员

324
00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:24.840
is showing up.
出现了。

325
00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:26.440
I did a Sunday show with him.
我和他一起做过周日的演出。

326
00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:28.880
And he'd be like, did you do improv with Amanda Love?
他会问，你和Amanda Love一起做过即兴表演吗？

327
00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.520
I'm like, yes, Rainn.
我说，是的，Rainn。

328
00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:34.260
Well, Rainn and I were the two classically trained theater actors.
嗯，Rainn和我当时是组里唯二受过古典戏剧训练的演员。

329
00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:35.220
Oh, don't we know it?
哦，我们难道不知道吗？

330
00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:35.560
In the group.
在那个组里。

331
00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:36.860
Oh, don't we know it?
哦，我们难道不知道吗？

332
00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:39.060
I heard quite a bit about it.
我对此可是听过不少。

333
00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:39.460
Yes.
是的。

334
00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:40.160
All right.
好吧。

335
00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:43.660
Before things take a turn here, maybe we should go to a break.
在事情变得不可收拾之前，也许我们该休息一下了。

336
00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:44.660
Yeah, let's go to a break.
好的，我们去休息一下。

337
00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:52.740
And we're back talking about the sexual harassment episode.
我们回来了，继续讨论《性骚扰》那一集。

338
00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:53.920
Here we go.
开始了。

339
00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:54.680
Here we go.
开始了。

340
00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:55.880
Buckle in, everyone.
大家系好安全带。

341
00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:56.900
Buckle in, as they say.
正如他们所说，系好安全带。

342
00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.440
In rewatching this episode, Angela, I was very uncomfortable.
Angela，在重温这一集时，我感到非常不自在。

343
00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:02.380
Yeah.
是啊。

344
00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:07.100
I was more squirmy during this than Diversity Day.
比起《多元日》那一集，这一集让我更坐立难安。

345
00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.440
Well, yeah.
嗯，是啊。

346
00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:10.420
I mean, I don't know.
我是说，我不知道。

347
00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.280
They're both equally squirmy for me.
对我来说，它们让人尴尬的程度是一样的。

348
00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:14.460
But then I was squirmy during Hot Girl.
但我看《辣妹》那一集时也觉得很尴尬。

349
00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:21.960
I think that I had forgotten how really cringy and uncomfortable the show can get sometimes.
我想我忘了这部剧有时会变得多么令人尴尬和不适。

350
00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.200
Oh, we pushed it.
哦，我们确实做得过火了。

351
00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:26.020
We pushed it to the line and then went over the line.
我们当时把尺度推到了边缘，甚至越过了那条线。

352
00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:28.140
How did this show get on the air?
这档节目是怎么获准播出的？

353
00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:31.500
I mean, I know this particular episode got on with a warning.
我是说，我知道这一集是在有警告提示的情况下播出的。

354
00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:34.300
But in general, what was going on?
但总的来说，当时到底是怎么回事？

355
00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:35.040
I don't know.
我不知道。

356
00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:38.800
I mean, you know, I grew up overseas and I grew up with a lot of British television.
我是说，你知道的，我在海外长大，看了很多英国电视节目。

357
00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:41.320
And they definitely pushed the line.
它们确实突破了尺度。

358
00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:45.260
And I think the show was in the spirit of the BBC version.
我觉得这档节目很有BBC原版的精神。

359
00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:47.500
And I don't know.
我也不清楚。

360
00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:53.200
I think like some of the cringy moments that you end up laughing, I don't know.
我觉得就像那些让你尴尬到发笑的时刻，我不知道该怎么说。

361
00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:54.340
I love it.
我喜欢这样。

362
00:12:54.480 --> 00:13:00.460
I know that Kevin Reilly, who was at NBC at the time, was a huge champion for our show.
我知道当时在NBC工作的凯文·赖利（Kevin Reilly）是我们节目的头号支持者。

363
00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:03.020
I really credit him with us sticking around.
我真的认为我们能坚持下来多亏了他。

364
00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:04.100
He believed in us.
他相信我们。

365
00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:09.660
And there were a lot of people there who didn't get it and who didn't think that this was a good idea.
当时台里有很多人并不理解，也不觉得这是个好主意。

366
00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:10.660
No, it's true.
没错，是真的。

367
00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:11.760
He fought for us.
他为我们据理力争。

368
00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:18.320
And when we finally won an Emmy for Best Comedy Ensemble, we all went backstage for photos.
当我们最终获得艾美奖最佳喜剧类剧集群戏奖时，我们都去后台拍照了。

369
00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:22.740
And the guys, the cast, picked up Kevin Reilly up in the air.
然后大家，也就是演员们，把凯文·赖利高高举了起来。

370
00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:29.220
And that's the photo that was in the LA Times because we all knew that he put his neck on the line for us.
那张照片后来登在了《洛杉矶时报》上，因为我们都知道他为了我们冒了很大的风险。

371
00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:31.980
And I mean, I'll always be grateful to Kevin for that.
我是说，我会永远为此感激凯文。

372
00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:39.440
The episode begins with Michael walking up to Jim's desk to see if he has received his hilarious email forward.
这一集开头，迈克尔走到吉姆的办公桌前，想看看他有没有收到自己转发的那个搞笑邮件。

373
00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:43.380
Michael has a talking head where he declares himself the king of forwards.
迈克尔有个单人访谈镜头，自封为“转发之王”。

374
00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.260
And he says, that's how I like to do business.
他说，这就是我喜欢的做生意方式。

375
00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:45.660
Yeah.
是啊。

376
00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:54.480
I have a funny story about a behind-the-scenes moment that happened on set while we were filming a big group scene in the bullpen talking about these email forwards.
关于幕后有个趣事，当时我们正在办公区拍摄一场大群戏，讨论这些转发邮件。

377
00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:55.720
And...
然后……

378
00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:56.260
Was I there?
我在场吗？

379
00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.020
You were there.
你在场。

380
00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:57.740
Okay, remind me.
好吧，提醒我一下。

381
00:13:57.740 --> 00:13:58.340
Everyone was there.
大家都在场。

382
00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.100
Everyone was there.
大家都在场。

383
00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:01.040
Kelly was there still with an up-do.
凯莉当时还在梳着那个高发髻。

384
00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:03.980
When is the episode where Kelly becomes Mindy?
凯莉变成明迪（Mindy）风格是哪一集来着？

385
00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:04.980
Exactly.
没错。

386
00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:06.720
That's what we need to look for.
那正是我们需要找的。

387
00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:07.360
No.
不是。

388
00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:12.820
So this is an episode that John Krasinski and I will never forget because he about fell out of his chair.
所以这一集我和约翰·卡拉辛斯基（John Krasinski）永远不会忘记，因为他当时差点从椅子上摔下来。

389
00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:19.940
At 9 minutes, 16 seconds, we're talking about the email forwards, and Michael's really upset that they want him to stop doing this.
在9分16秒的时候，我们正在谈论转发邮件，迈克尔对他们要求他停止转发感到非常沮丧。

390
00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.480
And I say, I hate them.
我说，我讨厌这些邮件。

391
00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:27.180
You send me these filthy emails, and you say, forward them to 10 people, or you'll have bad luck.
你发给我这些肮脏的邮件，还说要转发给10个人，否则就会倒霉。

392
00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:27.880
Right?
对吧？

393
00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:28.220
Yeah.
是啊。

394
00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:28.800
That's my line.
那是我的台词。

395
00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:33.900
So we had been working on this scene for a while, and then we went to lunch, and we came back.
我们拍这场戏拍了很久，然后去吃了午饭，回来继续拍。

396
00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:37.700
Oh, that's always so hard to pick up a scene with lunch in between.
噢，中间隔了顿午饭后再接戏总是很难。

397
00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:38.280
Yes.
确实。

398
00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:40.980
And I think it was like around 3 o'clock in the afternoon.
我想当时大概是下午3点左右。

399
00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:43.200
Oh, everyone's real off at that time.
噢，那个时间点大家状态都很差。

400
00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:44.240
Everyone's a little tired.
大家都有些累了。

401
00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:45.920
People are a little bit more punchy.
大家都有点兴奋过头了。

402
00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:46.240
Yeah.
是啊。

403
00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.240
And we're in a big group scene.
而且我们正在拍一场大群戏。

404
00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:50.400
So here's the thing you should know about me.
所以关于我，有件事你们得知道。

405
00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:52.280
I was born in Louisiana.
我出生在路易斯安那州。

406
00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.000
My family's from Texas and Louisiana.
我的家人来自德克萨斯州和路易斯安那州。

407
00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:58.180
I have a really, really hard time saying a vowel in front of an L.
我真的、真的很难发好L前面的元音。

408
00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:06.060
And two times in my career on The Office, they almost dropped a line because I could not say it.
在《办公室》拍摄期间，有两次他们差点删掉我的台词，因为我实在说不出来。

409
00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:08.040
One time, they actually did.
有一次，他们真的删了。

410
00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:09.480
I'll save that story for later.
那个故事我以后再说。

411
00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:11.500
It was between Andy Bernard and myself.
那是安迪·伯纳德和我之间的一场戏。

412
00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:12.760
I couldn't say the line.
我就是说不出那句台词。

413
00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:17.100
I just kept sounding like such a hillbilly that they just dropped the line.
我听起来太像乡巴佬了，所以他们干脆把台词删了。

414
00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:20.020
But this line, I said, I hate them.
但这次这句台词，我说的是，我讨厌它们。

415
00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.940
You send me these filthy emails.
你发给我这些肮脏的邮件。

416
00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:26.860
And John about fell out of his chair, and he went, the South has arrived.
约翰差点从椅子上摔下来，他说，南方口音上线了。

417
00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:28.780
And I was like, what?
我当时就问，什么？

418
00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:29.200
What?
什么？

419
00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:30.160
I didn't even hear it.
我甚至都没听出来。

420
00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:30.980
He was like, Angela.
他说，安吉拉。

421
00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:34.000
And like eight of you turned and looked at me.
然后你们大概有八个人转过头看着我。

422
00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:36.180
And at the same time, you were like, you said filthy.
同时你们说，你刚才说了“肮脏”。

423
00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:37.320
Filthy.
肮脏。

424
00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:39.020
And I said, how do you say it?
我说，那你们怎么说这个词？

425
00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.680
And you're like, filthy.
你们说，肮脏。

426
00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:44.520
And I had to like really concentrate, filthy, filthy.
我不得不非常专注地练习，肮脏，肮脏。

427
00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:47.480
Because I automatically want to say filthy, filthy.
因为我本能地想说成“肮脏”，那种口音。

428
00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:52.080
But somewhere there's footage of me saying, you send me these filthy emails.
但某处肯定有我当时说“你发给我这些肮脏的邮件”的片段。

429
00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:54.880
And John lost it.
约翰当时笑疯了。

430
00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:58.460
You and John had a great relationship on the show.
你和约翰在剧里的关系很好。

431
00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:00.940
You guys were big brother, kid sister.
你们就像哥哥和妹妹一样。

432
00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.120
And it was so sweet.
那真的很温馨。

433
00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:04.720
I loved your banter.
我喜欢你们的互动。

434
00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:06.640
And I loved just, I don't know.
我就是喜欢，我不知道怎么说。

435
00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:07.720
You guys were really cute.
你们真的很可爱。

436
00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.020
You would tease one another.
你们会互相打趣。

437
00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:09.720
I know.
我知道。

438
00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:12.660
He felt like my big brother, even though he's like younger than me.
他给我的感觉就像我的大哥哥，尽管他其实比我小。

439
00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:12.960
Yes.
是的。

440
00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:13.840
But he did.
但他确实是。

441
00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:15.740
He felt like my big brother that I teased.
他就像那个会被我捉弄的大哥哥。

442
00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:16.620
And he loved it.
而且他很享受。

443
00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:19.500
When I slipped into Southern Drawl, he'd be like, well, hello.
每当我带出南方口音时，他就会说，哟，你好啊。

444
00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:21.260
He loved it.
他很喜欢那样。

445
00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:24.300
So next up, Todd Packer comes in the office.
接下来，托德·帕克来到了办公室。

446
00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:28.940
And boy, does Dave Koechner own a room when he enters that room.
天哪，戴夫·科克纳一进门就能镇住全场。

447
00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:29.340
Yes.
没错。

448
00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:33.740
Dave told me last night on the phone, he said, Todd Packer just comes in and blows up your
昨晚在电话里戴夫告诉我，他说，托德·帕克一进来就会炸毁你的

449
00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:34.080
world.
世界。

450
00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:35.420
And then kaboom, leaves.
然后砰的一声，就离开了。

451
00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:36.360
No consequences.
没有后果。

452
00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:37.160
Mic drop.
帅气离场。

453
00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:38.040
See you later.
回头见。

454
00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:38.820
And then he's out.
然后他就走了。

455
00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:41.280
I have a little tidbit about Dave.
关于戴夫，我有个小八卦。

456
00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:42.440
Oh, tell me.
哦，快告诉我。

457
00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:42.760
OK.
好。

458
00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:45.620
So Dave told me he actually auditioned for Michael Scott.
戴夫告诉我，他其实试镜过迈克尔·斯科特这个角色。

459
00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:46.240
What?
什么？

460
00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:46.820
Yes.
是的。

461
00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:49.020
He had known Greg Daniels for years.
他认识格雷格·丹尼尔斯很多年了。

462
00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:52.740
He had done a pilot for one of Greg's writers on King of the Hill.
他曾为格雷格在《乡巴佬希尔》的一位编剧试演过一部试播集。

463
00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:53.060
Yeah.
没错。

464
00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.160
So he knew Greg for a long time.
所以他认识格雷格很久了。

465
00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:57.160
And they brought him in for Michael Scott.
他们让他来试镜迈克尔·斯科特。

466
00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:01.780
And he said, Ange, I was obsessed with the BBC version.
他说，安吉，我当时对BBC原版剧集非常着迷。

467
00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:04.260
And all I had in my head was Ricky Gervais.
我脑子里全是瑞奇·热维斯的影子。

468
00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:06.500
I couldn't do it any other way.
我没法用别的方式来演。

469
00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:09.300
So he was doing a little bit of an impersonation of Ricky.
所以他当时是在模仿瑞奇。

470
00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:09.920
Yes.
是的。

471
00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.460
And I think a lot of people did that, that came in.
我想很多来试镜的人都这么做了。

472
00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:14.080
But Steve had not seen it.
但史蒂夫没看过原版。

473
00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:17.860
And I think that really helped him kind of make his own person.
我觉得这反而帮他塑造出了属于自己的角色。

474
00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:18.240
Yeah.
没错。

475
00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:22.100
But he told me when they brought him in for Todd Packer, he was so excited.
但他告诉我，当他们让他来试镜托德·帕克时，他非常兴奋。

476
00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:25.080
Because yes, it was based on Finchie, right, in the BBC version.
因为没错，这个角色是基于BBC原版里的芬奇设计的，对吧？

477
00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:25.400
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

478
00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:29.380
So in the BBC version, David Brent has a friend named Chris Finch.
在BBC原版里，大卫·布伦特有个朋友叫克里斯·芬奇。

479
00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.300
And they call him Finchie.
他们叫他芬奇。

480
00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:33.500
And he is the Todd Packer of the British show.
他就是英版里的托德·帕克。

481
00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.880
Basically, it's just this one-sided best friendship.
基本上，这就是一段单方面的“挚友”关系。

482
00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:40.740
And if you can believe, Chris Finch is worse than Todd Packer.
如果你敢相信的话，克里斯·芬奇比托德·帕克还要糟糕。

483
00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:41.240
He is worse.
他更糟糕。

484
00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:45.240
If you watch the British show, you think it can't get worse than Todd Packer.
如果你看过英版，你会觉得没人能比托德·帕克更烂了。

485
00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:48.260
Or if you're looking for that, check out the British version.
或者如果你想见识一下，可以去看看英版。

486
