1282
00:48:13.590 --> 00:48:18.050
Jenna's Pam document wasn't given to her by Greg Daniels or any writers or producers.
珍娜的这份“潘”档案并不是格雷格·丹尼尔斯或者任何编剧、制片人给她的。

1283
00:48:18.050 --> 00:48:22.370
This was a document that Jenna made herself for her character.
这是珍娜为了自己的角色亲自制作的文档。

1284
00:48:22.570 --> 00:48:25.230
These are the kinds of things you learn in theater school, Angela.
安吉拉，这些都是你在戏剧学校里学到的东西。

1285
00:48:26.950 --> 00:48:28.530
You can suck it.
去你的吧。

1286
00:48:29.490 --> 00:48:31.630
These are the things we're encouraged to do.
这些都是我们被鼓励去做的事情。

1287
00:48:31.630 --> 00:48:32.710
I took some theater.
我学过一些戏剧。

1288
00:48:33.090 --> 00:48:34.470
I took theater classes.
我上过戏剧课。

1289
00:48:34.670 --> 00:48:36.630
You know, just trained theater actors are encouraged.
你知道的，受过专业训练的戏剧演员都会被这样鼓励。

1290
00:48:36.630 --> 00:48:39.930
I took classes at HB Studios in New York City.
我在纽约市的HB工作室上过课。

1291
00:48:40.170 --> 00:48:40.490
Okay.
好吧。

1292
00:48:40.670 --> 00:48:43.790
With Carol Rosenfeld, who was a protégé of Uta Hagen.
是跟卡罗尔·罗森菲尔德学的，她是乌塔·哈根的学生。

1293
00:48:43.970 --> 00:48:45.150
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

1294
00:48:45.230 --> 00:48:45.530
All right.
行吧。

1295
00:48:45.670 --> 00:48:46.510
That's some pedigree.
那可是名门出身啊。

1296
00:48:46.710 --> 00:48:47.190
Thank you.
谢谢。

1297
00:48:47.290 --> 00:48:47.650
All right.
好吧。

1298
00:48:48.050 --> 00:48:48.750
I got a blessing.
我得到认可了。

1299
00:48:49.030 --> 00:48:49.190
Oh.
噢。

1300
00:48:49.750 --> 00:48:55.810
Well, in my document, I had asked myself the question, how did Pam and Roy end up together anyway?
嗯，在我的文档里，我问过自己一个问题：潘和罗伊到底是怎么走到一起的？

1301
00:48:56.210 --> 00:49:00.710
So I've answered sort of why I think they're still together, but how did they end up together?
我已经回答了为什么我认为他们还在一起，但他们是怎么走到一起的呢？

1302
00:49:01.010 --> 00:49:02.850
They seem so mismatched to me.
在我看来他们太不般配了。

1303
00:49:03.090 --> 00:49:03.970
Here was my backstory.
这是我的背景故事。

1304
00:49:04.570 --> 00:49:10.990
Pam's family owned an appliance shop in downtown Scranton, like in the town square.
帕姆的家人在斯克兰顿市中心，也就是城镇广场那边，开了一家电器店。

1305
00:49:12.250 --> 00:49:18.530
Roy, in high school, got a job working at the appliance store, and he was a great worker.
罗伊高中时在电器店找了份工作，他是个很棒的员工。

1306
00:49:18.690 --> 00:49:22.670
He was very charming, as in the Roy you just saw here in the sweater.
他非常有魅力，就像你刚才看到的那个穿毛衣的罗伊一样。

1307
00:49:22.670 --> 00:49:30.810
And so that was how their worlds collided, because Pam was probably this little nerdy art student in high school.
所以他们的世界就是这样碰撞在一起的，因为帕姆在高中时可能只是个书呆子艺术生。

1308
00:49:30.810 --> 00:49:32.950
So I couldn't figure out how did she meet Roy.
所以我一直想不通她是怎么认识罗伊的。

1309
00:49:33.170 --> 00:49:34.510
Who was probably a jock.
他可能是个运动健将。

1310
00:49:34.610 --> 00:49:34.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1311
00:49:35.090 --> 00:49:35.290
Yeah.
没错。

1312
00:49:35.290 --> 00:49:36.410
And this was how.
原因就是这样。

1313
00:49:36.570 --> 00:49:39.990
He was very charming, and he asked her out, and they started dating.
他非常有魅力，他约她出去，然后他们就开始约会了。

1314
00:49:40.210 --> 00:49:43.570
But because he worked there, like the families became very enmeshed.
但因为他在那儿工作，两家人的关系变得非常紧密。

1315
00:49:43.750 --> 00:49:44.970
They would barbecue together.
他们会一起烧烤。

1316
00:49:45.290 --> 00:49:52.890
So this is why and how she kind of can't get out of this relationship, even though now it's clear it's a mismatch.
所以这就是为什么她有点无法摆脱这段关系，尽管现在很明显他们并不般配。

1317
00:49:53.370 --> 00:49:57.090
It's because the families are so cojoined.
因为两家人的关系已经深度捆绑了。

1318
00:49:57.570 --> 00:50:06.530
And do you think that Pam decided not to work at the appliance store and go out, branch out, and then Roy followed her to the warehouse?
你觉得是不是帕姆决定不去电器店工作，想出去闯闯，然后罗伊就跟着她去了仓库？

1319
00:50:06.830 --> 00:50:08.130
Oh, my gosh, Angela.
天哪，安吉拉。

1320
00:50:08.270 --> 00:50:12.230
I don't know, but I feel like I'm going to go back and put that in my document right now.
我不知道，但我感觉我现在就要回去把这一点写进我的文档里。

1321
00:50:12.470 --> 00:50:16.590
Because here's Pam, like, okay, I'm not going to work at the family business.
因为帕姆当时的想法是，好吧，我不想在家族企业工作了。

1322
00:50:16.770 --> 00:50:18.130
I need some space.
我需要一点空间。

1323
00:50:18.130 --> 00:50:20.190
I need to figure out who I am.
我需要弄清楚我是谁。

1324
00:50:20.310 --> 00:50:20.750
Yes.
没错。

1325
00:50:20.750 --> 00:50:23.070
And then Roy's like, hey, I got a job at that warehouse.
然后罗伊就说，嘿，我在那个仓库找了份工作。

1326
00:50:23.070 --> 00:50:24.930
We'll be able to see each other every day.
这样我们就能每天见面了。

1327
00:50:25.270 --> 00:50:26.310
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1328
00:50:26.530 --> 00:50:32.310
I find it interesting that Pam eats in the break room with Jim and not in the warehouse with Roy.
我觉得很有意思的一点是，帕姆是和吉姆在休息室吃饭，而不是和罗伊在仓库吃。

1329
00:50:32.510 --> 00:50:34.850
Now, we see Roy sometimes eat there.
当然，我们有时也会看到罗伊在那里吃。

1330
00:50:35.010 --> 00:50:36.330
Yeah, they don't eat lunch together, do they?
是啊，他们不一起吃午饭，对吧？

1331
00:50:36.330 --> 00:50:37.610
Not very often.
不常一起吃。

1332
00:50:39.210 --> 00:50:45.550
And then Pam's mom has the moment in this episode where she whispers, which one is Jim?
然后帕姆的妈妈在这一集里有个瞬间，她低声问，哪一个是吉姆？

1333
00:50:45.890 --> 00:50:48.030
And you see John Krasinski's face.
你看到了约翰·卡拉辛斯基的表情。

1334
00:50:48.030 --> 00:50:59.230
He's all pleased that he knows now that Pam – and by the way, in casino night, we know Pam calls her mom on the phone to, you know, share about what happened in the parking lot.
他很高兴，因为他现在知道帕姆——顺便说一下，在赌场之夜那集，我们知道帕姆给妈妈打了电话，分享了停车场发生的事。

1335
00:50:59.450 --> 00:51:06.570
Well, I just love the moment, and John played it so well, where he sees his opportunity to introduce himself to Pam's mom.
我真的很喜欢那个瞬间，约翰演得太好了，他看到了向帕姆妈妈介绍自己的机会。

1336
00:51:06.570 --> 00:51:14.350
And he gets up the courage, and he walks over right as Roy walks in, and he just quickly takes, like, a piece of candy and goes back to his desk.
他鼓起勇气走过去，正好罗伊走了进来，他只好迅速拿了块糖，又回到了自己的座位上。

1337
00:51:15.030 --> 00:51:16.910
And that kind of broke my heart for him.
那一幕让我为他感到心碎。

1338
00:51:17.150 --> 00:51:25.790
Lastly, from Dave Koechner, who plays Todd Packer, he said, Ange, please let everyone know I am nothing like Todd Packer in real life.
最后，饰演托德·帕克的戴夫·科克纳说，安吉，请告诉大家，我在现实生活中一点也不像托德·帕克。

1339
00:51:25.790 --> 00:51:27.870
Oh, and it's true, everyone.
噢，这是真的，大家。

1340
00:51:28.190 --> 00:51:28.630
I know.
我知道。

1341
00:51:28.850 --> 00:51:33.950
Dave is just a sweet, sweet, sweetheart, father of five.
戴夫是个非常甜、非常甜、非常贴心的人，还是五个孩子的父亲。

1342
00:51:34.150 --> 00:51:34.510
I know.
我知道。

1343
00:51:34.550 --> 00:51:37.690
And he said, he goes, I just wish you and Jenna all the beSt.
他说，他祝愿你和珍娜一切都好。

1344
00:51:37.790 --> 00:51:38.990
This is such a great idea.
这真是个好主意。

1345
00:51:38.990 --> 00:51:40.850
I just love it as a fan of the show.
作为这部剧的粉丝，我太喜欢了。

1346
00:51:41.030 --> 00:51:45.490
It's got to be hard to believe that he is not like Todd Packer for some people.
对有些人来说，要相信他不像托德·帕克一定很难。

1347
00:51:45.490 --> 00:51:52.530
To imagine that if you met him, he is just the warmest, nicest, wonderful gentleman.
想象一下，如果你见到他，他是一个最热情、最友善、最棒的绅士。

1348
00:51:52.770 --> 00:51:53.250
I know.
我知道。

1349
00:51:53.430 --> 00:51:57.290
Yeah, I think sometimes you get known as this character, but he's nothing like that.
是啊，我觉得有时候你会因为某个角色而被定型，但他本人完全不是那样。

1350
00:51:57.350 --> 00:51:58.870
I'm nothing like Angela Martin.
我也一点都不像安吉拉·马丁。

1351
00:51:59.130 --> 00:51:59.750
This is true.
这是真的。

1352
00:52:00.050 --> 00:52:01.530
You're a little bit like Pam.
你有点像帕姆。

1353
00:52:01.870 --> 00:52:02.530
I am.
我是。

1354
00:52:02.670 --> 00:52:04.750
All right, guys, that was sexual harassment.
好了，各位，刚才那是性骚扰。

1355
00:52:04.910 --> 00:52:06.050
That was sexual harassment.
刚才那是性骚扰。

1356
00:52:06.050 --> 00:52:06.830
We did it.
我们做到了。

1357
00:52:06.990 --> 00:52:11.790
Next week is Office Olympics with special guest director Paul Feig.
下周是办公室奥运会，特邀客座导演保罗·费格。

1358
00:52:11.890 --> 00:52:15.330
He is the best-dressed man in show business, for sure.
他绝对是演艺圈里最会穿衣服的男人。

1359
00:52:15.490 --> 00:52:16.250
Go to his Instagram.
去看看他的Instagram吧。

1360
00:52:16.610 --> 00:52:17.270
It is delightful.
非常赏心悦目。

1361
00:52:18.590 --> 00:52:20.610
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1362
